        <section id="coding-features" >
          
            <h2>Coding features</h2>
              <p>To show how the code looks, we are going to show three general features which are common to all code in each language:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Comments:</strong> sections of code to inform the programmer which are ignored by the program</li>
<li><strong>A variable declaration:</strong> variables are containers for data. A declaration is where one is introduced for the first time in a program.</li>
<li><strong>Printing an output to the console:</strong> a console is text interface from which inputs/outputs can be managed when a program is run. A “print” statement is a simple operation where an output is printed to the console.</li>
</ol>
<p>Please see in the below activity how these features differ according to each language:</p>


